{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/438140/", "pk": 438140, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/", "pk": 79348, "shortname": "bostonbyfoot", "name": "Boston By Foot", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Private Tour: Jewish Beacon Hill", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 10, "unicode": "Private Tour: Jewish Beacon Hill", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": true, "sold_out_text": "SOLD OUT!", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 336.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": false, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 336.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": false, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": true, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 50750, "description": "*From April to mid-November, Private tours of the 90min Jewish Beacon Hill walking tour are bookable online for groups of up to 20 people with at least 2 weeks notice. To request a private tour for groups of more than 20 people, or in the fall/winter, or that includes a visit to the Vilna Shul please use the Private Tour Request form. Please provide at least 3 weeks notice in advance of your preferred tour date for larger groups or special requests.*\n\n[Private tour request form link](https://form.jotform.com/220595239082054)\n\n##Duration, Distance, Terrain\n1.5 hours\n1 mile at a moderate pace, stopping at various sites along the tour\nNote: This is an outdoor walking tour of the neighborhood. It does not include a tour of the Vilna Shul.\n\n##About\nJourney to Beacon Hill’s North Slope at the turn of the 20th century.\n\nExplore the lives of its Jewish residents during a period of cultural and architectural change.\n\nUncover how Boston’s Jewish immigrants created an active community that blended customs from Eastern Europe and changes to the new world around them.\n\nDiscover sites where Boston’s Jewish West End residents worked, lived and worshiped, including the sites of three synagogues within a few blocks of each other.    \n\n##Meeting location:\nMeet your guide in front of the Vilna Shul at 18 Phillips Street.\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest MBTA Stations: Charles/MGH (Red Line) & Bowdoin (Blue Line)\n\n##What to bring\nComfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "For tours that include only the Boston By Foot 90min walking tour, please meet your guide outside of the Vilna Shul.\n\nFor 2hr Jewish History tours that include both the Boston By Foot 90min walking tour and a 30min tour of the Vilna Shul, \n- Please meet your guide inside of the Vilna Shul\n- The Vilna Shul partners with a parking garage to offer validated discount parking. For more information please visit the Vilna Shul website: [The Vilna Shul Getting Here] (https://www.vilnashul.org/visit/location)", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Explore the history of Beacon Hill's Jewish community • 1.5 Hours", "short_description": "", "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/438140/images/900084/", "pk": 900084, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/w9N2WDuSagWHNHocSKCw", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/w9N2WDuS